<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Military Dictatorship of Mughan</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1919 CE · capital Lankaran</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived regime of Russian settlers in the Mughan steppe of south-eastern Azerbaijan, which resisted the Azerbaijan Democratic Republic in 1918-1919.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Mughan steppe and Lankaran area had many Russian settler villages, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molokans">Molokans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-believers">Old Believers</a>, established in the 19th century. When the Russian administration collapsed in 1918, local settlers and former Russian officers formed their own armed government at Lankaran rather than accept the new Azerbaijani state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The regime was run by Russian officers and settler councils as a military administration, aligned with the anti-Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">White movement</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/russian-state">Russian State</a> and receiving some British and White support. It controlled the Russian villages and fought local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talysh">Talysh</a> and Azerbaijani forces loyal to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan-democratic-republic">Azerbaijan Democratic Republic</a>. Little is known of its internal administration beyond military rule.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In spring 1919 a regional congress of Mughan settlers turned against the military leadership, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> took power, proclaiming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mughan-soviet-republic">Mughan Soviet Republic</a>. The region was soon brought under Azerbaijani control.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-military-dictatorship-of-mughan.jpg" alt="Provisional Military Dictatorship of Mughan" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Peter the Great · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Russia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lankaran</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Russian Orthodox Christianity; Molokan and Old Believer communities</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mughan Provisional Military Government, Mughan Territory</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=provisional-military-dictatorship-of-mughan" aria-label="Provisional Military Dictatorship of Mughan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5892 787 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Military Dictatorship of Mughan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6212 1043L6611 554M6212 1043L6212 1043"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6611 554h0M6212 1043h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6212 1043h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6212 1043h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lankaran. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=provisional-military-dictatorship-of-mughan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
